@startuml
title Bridge Pattern in Java
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
top to bottom direction

abstract class Shape {
  # x : double {readOnly}
  # y : double {readOnly}
  - renderer : Renderer
  # Shape(x, y, renderer)
  + setRenderer(renderer : Renderer) : void
  # getRenderer() : Renderer
  # {static} requirePositive(value, name) : double
  - {static} requireFinite(value, name) : double
  + {abstract} draw() : void
}
class Circle {
  - radius : double {readOnly}
  + Circle(x, y, radius, renderer)
  + draw() : void
}
class Square {
  - side : double {readOnly}
  + Square(x, y, side, renderer)
  + draw() : void
}
interface Renderer {
  + renderCircle(x, y, radius) : void
  + renderLine(startX, startY, endX, endY) : void
}
class VectorRenderer {
  + renderCircle(x, y, radius) : void
  + renderLine(startX, startY, endX, endY) : void
}
class RasterRenderer {
  + renderCircle(x, y, radius) : void
  + renderLine(startX, startY, endX, endY) : void
}
class Main {
  + {static} main(args : String[]) : void
  - {static} demonstrateSwitch(name, shape, replacement) : void
}

Shape <|-- Circle
Shape <|-- Square
Renderer <|.. VectorRenderer
Renderer <|.. RasterRenderer
Shape o--> "1" Renderer : renderer / bridge
Main ..> Shape : uses
Main ..> VectorRenderer : creates
Main ..> RasterRenderer : creates
note bottom of Shape
Object composition: a shape holds a renderer.
Hollow diamond = shared reference, as in the lecture.
Renderer lifetime is not owned exclusively by one shape.
end note
@enduml
